    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Avial"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is one of the essential dishes on a Kerala "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "avial",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "avial"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " table. It appears at the Onam "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "sadya",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "sadya"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " feast, alongside rice and sambar. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "coconut oil finish",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "coconut-oil-finish"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is not optional. It gives the dish its characteristic Kerala flavour and should be added just before serving."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cut all vegetables to a uniform size so they cook at the same rate. Avoid overcooking: the vegetables should hold their shape, not become a mash."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
